# AEGIS — End-to-End Two-Node Connectivity Implementation and Verification

## Role

Act as a senior distributed-systems engineer, TypeScript/Node.js systems architect, networking engineer, and test automation engineer.

You are working on the existing AEGIS monorepo. Your task is to inspect, debug, repair, implement, and verify the complete peer-to-peer networking pipeline so that two independent AEGIS nodes can establish a connection, authenticate their identities, exchange application messages bidirectionally, detect disconnections, and reconnect reliably.

Do not merely provide recommendations or generate a plan. Work directly in the repository, make the necessary code changes, execute the available tests, and report the actual results.

**Primary objective: prove that two distinct AEGIS nodes can communicate end to end.**

Do not claim success unless supported by executed tests and observable evidence.

