## 8. Phase Seven — Verify LAN Discovery Separately

Manual peer connectivity and automatic peer discovery are separate capabilities.

Test them independently.

For LAN discovery:

1. Start two nodes on the same supported network.
2. Confirm both announce their canonical identities and reachable endpoints.
3. Confirm the discovery listener receives and validates announcements.
4. Confirm discovered endpoints are registered correctly.
5. Confirm a discovered peer can establish the normal authenticated handshake.
6. Confirm stale peers expire or are removed according to the existing discovery design.
7. Confirm duplicate announcements do not create duplicate peer records.
8. Test interface selection and firewall restrictions.

Do not assume UDP broadcast works across subnets, VPNs, Wi-Fi client isolation, or routers.

If discovery is unavailable, manual registration must still be able to establish a connection when the remote endpoint is reachable.

